# There is no billing and no identity provider to configure. Authentication is
# one API key, generated on first run and written to $SANDBOXD_DATA/bootstrap.key
# — see the README's self-hosting section. Nothing below is required for a
# single node except a data directory.

# ─── Required (Production) ────────────────────────────────────
DATABASE_URL=postgres://sandbox:sandbox_dev@localhost:5432/sandbox?sslmode=disable

# ─── Optional (with defaults) ────────────────────────────────
PORT=8080
SNAPSHOT_DIR=/var/lib/sandbox/templates
OVERLAY_DIR=/var/lib/sandbox/overlays
FIRECRACKER_BIN=/usr/bin/firecracker
JAILER_BIN=/usr/bin/jailer
KERNEL_PATH=/var/lib/sandbox/vmlinux

# ─── Dev Server Only ─────────────────────────────────────────
# MAX_SANDBOXES=20
# ENVD_BIN=./bin/envd-local

# ─── Python SDK / CLI ────────────────────────────────────────
PILLDROPS_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
PILLDROPS_API_KEY=
# E2B_API_URL / E2B_API_KEY are read as fallbacks, so code written
# against the E2B SDK runs here unchanged.

# ─── AI Agent (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Agent Workstation
#
# Everything below is OPTIONAL. Each block degrades to a defined, VISIBLE state
# when unset — not a crash, and not a silent no-op. An unconfigured deployment
# must still run, and must tell you what it is not doing.
#
# Rotate anything that has ever been pasted into a chat, a ticket or a
# screenshot. A key is only secret until it is convenient.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Workstation durability (internal/daemon) ────────────────
# Durable home for pause snapshots, OFF the node's own disk. A paused
# workstation's snapshot IS the customer's machine; without this, losing the
# node loses their work permanently and silently. Point at a mounted network
# volume. Unset = node-local only — fine for dev, not for anything paid.
# SNAPSHOT_ARCHIVE_DIR=/mnt/snapshots

# How long a persistent workstation may sit unused before it is destroyed.
# Set in code (30 days); listed here so the number is discoverable.

# ─── Mobile bridge (internal/tgbridge) ───────────────────────
# From @BotFather. Unset = the bridge does not start, cleanly.
# Verified with getMe at boot, so a bad token is reported at startup rather than
# failing invisibly every 30 seconds.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Bot handle, for one-tap t.me deep links. Unset = the user retypes a code,
# which is the step people abandon.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME=
# Where the bridge drives sandboxes. Default is the orchestrator's own /v1,
# which is right in production; override to point a dev bridge at one sandboxd.
# BRIDGE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# BRIDGE_API_KEY=
#
# Voice notes are transcribed INSIDE the customer's workstation with the
# provider key already in that sandbox's env — so there is deliberately no
# transcription key here. We never hold a customer credential and never see
# their transcription bill. Voice needs OPENAI_API_KEY in the workstation.

# ─── Analytics (internal/webui) — recommended: Plausible ─────
# No cookies, so no consent banner; one script tag; self-hostable later by
# changing ANALYTICS_SRC alone.
#
# The tag is injected at SERVE time, not pasted into ~30 HTML files: a page
# added tomorrow is measured without anyone remembering, and a page silently
# missing analytics is how a bake-off compares four numbers and one blank.
#
# Setup: plausible.io -> add site -> use the domain exactly as registered.
# Unset = no third-party script at all.
# ANALYTICS_DOMAIN=example.com
# ANALYTICS_SRC=https://plausible.io/js/script.js
#
# The half that matters needs no vendor: the activation funnel
# (signup -> created -> alive at 24h) is computed from the database at
# GET /v1/admin/funnel?days=21. Pageviews say what attracts; that says what was real.

# ─── Marketing pages (internal/webui) ────────────────────────
# Serve marketing HTML from disk instead of the binary, so a headline change is
# a file write rather than a Go rebuild and a redeploy. Only slugs already in
# webui.PublicPages are overridable. Unset = embedded, exactly as before.
# PILLDROPS_PAGES_DIR=/srv/pilldrops/pages
# PILLDROPS_DL_DIR=

